      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30-90 days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5 · 2026-08-16-israel-strikes-iranian-territory-by-sep30</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Israeli forces conduct a TIER1-confirmed airstrike on targets physically located inside Iranian territory (within Iran's internationally recognized borders) before EOD 2026-09-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">48%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New today</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. The June 2026 ceasefire collapsed July 8; Israel-Hezbollah exchanges in Lebanon resumed and escalated through August. IDF conducted its deadliest Lebanon strikes since late June on August 15 (11+ killed, Radwan Force commander killed per Al Jazeera/Times of Israel). Iran struck a UAE oil vessel in Hormuz on August 15 and has attacked shipping repeatedly since July. Trump's August 14 Hormuz territorial claim alters US strategic posture. Prior base rate: two rounds of direct Israel-Iran strikes occurred in this conflict cycle (Twelve-Day War February 2026; June 13-14 exchange). The 45-day window is long enough to capture at least one significant escalation event if the Hormuz crisis deepens. P set near even reflecting the conflict's active trajectory and prior strike cadence.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if two independent TIER1 sources (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN/Al Jazeera) OR one TIER1 plus an official IDF statement confirm Israeli airstrikes on targets physically located inside Iran's internationally recognized land borders between 2026-08-16 and 2026-09-30.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two independent TIER1 OR IDF statement + one TIER1. IRGC or Iranian state media statement alone does NOT resolve — Iranian military communiqués have been contradicted by TIER1 in this conflict.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Israeli strikes in Lebanon, Syria, Iraq, or international waters against IRGC-linked targets do NOT count — must be physically inside Iranian territory. Strikes on Iranian-flagged vessels in international waters do NOT count. Israeli strikes on Iranian proxies operating from non-Iranian soil do NOT count.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IDF announces kinetic operation against targets inside Iranian territory (+50pp if observed)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">TIER1 reports large-scale Israeli air activity in eastern direction or Iranian air defense activation inside Iran (+20pp if observed)</span>
        </div>
