      </div>

      <div class="regime-row">
        <span class="name">🇮🇱 Israel (Netanyahu Steps Down)</span>
        <span class="p">30–45%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Election date set October 27; Knesset dissolved July 17 (62-0). Netanyahu running again as Likud head. Polling aggregates show right-wing bloc at 55-60 seats — below the 61-seat majority in most surveys. If the right bloc fails to form a coalition, Netanyahu's Likud leadership is at risk in the post-election negotiation period. The 30-45% range captures both the scenario of a narrow bloc win enabling Netanyahu continuity and the scenario of an opposition government requiring his departure from leadership. Updated this Sunday; next review 2026-08-23.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
